From 74ac986ec523f1990bce9d1e2732eb4753dbcbcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:54:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add an isolated manifest-driven V2 development command to
 lotusd

Provide explicit status, complete-block submit and guarded disconnect commands before inherited chain initialization. Require an isolated marked data namespace and caller-supplied manifest; start no sockets or Chronik. Strict numeric/profile parsing, local capacity bounds and poisoned-store reporting preserve operational error distinctions. Offline daemon checks accept the proposed first block with Python-reference identity/state root, reopen, disconnect/reconnect and reject malformed data without mutation. Preserve legacy-looking directories. Include explicit artifact conversion and reproducible process-level checks; no profile adoption or public testnet claim.
